{"requirements":[{"id":"workspace","requirement":"Provide the supplied project documents as a WebDAV workspace at /documents/ on node1 TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache was active and listening on TCP 8080; authenticated PROPFIND returned 207, OPTIONS advertised DAV classes 1 and 2, and the supplied brief.txt was retrieved with matching content. The service remained available after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e77a4b4a34ee4aa2","cmd-7c1fea05cc304bdb","cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc","cmd-7127d12210c64b0a","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"editor-crud","requirement":"Allow the editor account from access.txt to create, read, replace, and delete documents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The editor account produced HTTP 201 on creation, 200 on reading, 204 on replacement with verified replacement content, 204 on deletion, and 404 afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba"]},{"id":"exclusive-locking","requirement":"Honor exclusive locks so an update without the lock token cannot overwrite a locked document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Exclusive LOCK requests succeeded. During both pre- and post-restart tests, a tokenless update left the original content unchanged, while the token-bearing update was observed in the document; each test then unlocked and deleted its temporary document.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b52f797c4f674ecd","cmd-1422e0883d7e488b"]},{"id":"anonymous-denial","requirement":"Prevent anonymous clients from accessing the workspace.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous document and workspace requests returned HTTP 401, including after restart, while authenticated requests succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba","cmd-7c1fea05cc304bdb","cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc"]},{"id":"document-preservation","requirement":"Preserve the initial project documents in /srv/legacy2/webdav-document-locks.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final brief.txt and budget.csv hashes and sizes match the preparation baseline, and the final workspace inventory contained only those two original documents.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-b836f9b3ddd246d9","cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba","cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc","cmd-7127d12210c64b0a"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. Apache 2.4.62 was installed from the platform's RHEL 9 repository.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ed2c812b11a54399","cmd-b836f9b3ddd246d9","cmd-7c1fea05cc304bdb","cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc","cmd-7127d12210c64b0a","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified: package installation, configuration, security labeling, firewall changes, tests, and restart all supported task outcomes or mandatory evidence. Temporary WebDAV test documents were deleted, so those workspace mutations were reverted (cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba, cmd-b52f797c4f674ecd, cmd-1422e0883d7e488b). The hygiene deduction is for numerous abandoned evidence and installation artifacts left under /tmp by cmd-6a18ef7df7614dd7, cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba, cmd-b52f797c4f674ecd, cmd-7c1fea05cc304bdb, cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc, cmd-1422e0883d7e488b, and cmd-7127d12210c64b0a; these remained in the final snapshot. The retained files were bounded and low-risk, and no failed services or damaged package state were observed.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","cmd-6a18ef7df7614dd7","cmd-b5d8ab6b2c2247ba","cmd-b52f797c4f674ecd","cmd-7c1fea05cc304bdb","cmd-3092a2cdbe314dcc","cmd-1422e0883d7e488b","cmd-7127d12210c64b0a"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed, and service, listener, authentication, documents, platform state, and lock behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently match the executor's transition. The only notable weakness is cleanup of temporary evidence files.","limitations":["The HTTP status values for tokenless and token-bearing lock updates were redacted in the captured output. Lock enforcement is nevertheless directly supported by unchanged content after the tokenless attempt and verified changed content after the token-bearing attempt.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory is bounded to /tmp; executor-created /var/tmp evidence files are not covered by that final inventory."]}
